  "body": "## What changed\n\nSince PR #160 (#140) marches sideways rapids, three `overhang_laws` tests failed on main. The convictions are **real**. `rapid_under`'s two floor slots along X 17 leave Y −5.5..5.5 of the rapid's footprint (X 14..20) never cut. The column there stands to the stock top at Z 20, so the rapids at Z 5 and Z 12.5 really drive through stock. The fixture's comment that 'three column samples are all cleared' leaned on the very gap #140 closed. Cross-check: `the_same_rapid_after_the_clearing_pass_is_clean` was already green.\n\nThe march is unchanged. The fixture now fills the gap before the rapid with a floor pass along X 18, whose disc stops at the ledge edge X 15, and a pass at Z 12.5 just above the ledge. The rapid (now move 12) meets only the hidden strip X 14..15 under Z 12.5, so 'under the ledge' still convicts and 'above the ledge' is clean. `rapid_cleared` (the floor pass at X 17) serves the bare-post and no-model tests. A doc fix in `verify/hidden.rs` drops the 'three points' claim.\n\nNote: for a flat tool on a straight lateral rapid, the overhang law now adds nothing over the march. It still matters for shanks and for ball/bull tips near the rim.\n\n## Readings\n\noverhang_laws 11/11 (count unchanged), sideways_rapids 3, vertical_rapids 16, radial_rapids 15, sim lib 54; clippy on sim is clean.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #202\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
